  "visual_observations": [
    "All nine requested later identities share a golden fresh Power surface, have intermediate development at half maturity and distinguish their mature silhouettes and pigments.",
    "Axial crown, lower axial rear point and separate side horns remain attached around the original block head, with clear facial pixels. No blocking exposed-geometry or cap-paint bleed appeared in selected comparisons.",
    "Run keeps upper/lower backward-downward points; Power keeps robust upward crown and side horns; Swim flattens crown backward with small horizontal side horns; compatible pairs moderate their inputs.",
    "Crown and side-horn caps are visible above across all nine forms; original skull paint remains plain, with no copied Run forehead stripe pattern.",
    "Image handedness matches: native right faces right with front toes onright and tail onleft, matching source side. Native left faces left."
  ],
  "approximations": [
    "Mature Fly native crown is nearly upright/back-leaning with a small forward terminal cap; source has a stronger overall upward-forward curl. Exact source forward sweep is not matched.",
    "Native side horns are shorter/blunter, crown and rear tips are closed cuboids, and the articulated body is slimmer with square feet/tail. Source skull stretching is represented around a fixed cube.",
    "Native lighting is darker/flatter. Pixel cap/rim accents simplify source zigzag/tapered regions.",
    "The viewer side is slightly oblique with an eye visible; native exact side hides the planar face. Idle head lean, arm pose and blink phase differ.",
